00:51:56,666 --> 00:52:02,666
Abigail Leigh Spencer (born August 4, 1981) is an
American actress, producer and writer.

12
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
She began her career playing Rebecca Tyree on the ABC daytime television soap opera All My Children
(1999–2001) before going on to star in the Lifetime crime drama series, Angela's Eyes (2006).

13
01:01:23,333 --> 01:01:29,333
From 2013 to 2016, Spencer starred as Amantha Holden in the SundanceTV drama series Rectify, for which she received a nomination for a
Critics' Choice Television Award; she then starred as history professor Lucy Preston in the NBC science-fiction series Timeless.

14
01:06:06,666 --> 01:06:12,666
In 2026 she aired in a lead role in the FOX series Best Medicine.

15
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:56,000
Spencer has appeared in many films, including In My Sleep (2010), Cowboys & Aliens (2011), This Means War (2012), Chasing Mavericks (2012), The
Haunting in Connecticut 2: Ghosts of Georgia (2013), Oz the Great and Powerful (2013), and This Is Where I Leave You (2014).

16
01:15:33,333 --> 01:15:39,333
She also had recurring roles on the series Mad Men (2009), Hawthorne
(2009–2011), Suits (2011–2019), and Grey's Anatomy (2017–2022).

